  "geometryBasis": "The named industrial site identifies the plant, three circular polygons map the cooling towers, and four mapped visible chimneys corroborate the federal aerial. The principal visible roof volumes follow broad shape controls from the public-domain federal orthophoto.",
  "sectionBasis": "The historical operator journal gives two 435-ft cooling towers and the largest as 492 ft. It records the two original 900-ft chimneys and approximate diameters. The modern permit document gives the same height for the newer pair. NARA photographs show the tapered concrete forms and characteristic riverside silhouette.",
